{"name":"Open Range","hex":"#91876b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"open","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Physically unobstructed, uncovered, etc.\nAble to have something pass through or along it.","Able to have something pass through or along it."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make or become physically unobstructed, uncovered, etc.\n To make or become accessible or clear for passage by moving from a shut position.","To make or become accessible or clear for passage by moving from a shut position."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/open"},{"term":"range","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A line or series of mountains, buildings, etc.","A fireplace; a fire or other cooking apparatus; now specifically, a large cooking stove with many burners (hotplates)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To travel over (an area, etc); to roam, wander. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To rove over or through."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/range"}],"entries":[{"title":"Open range","blocks":[{"text":"In the Western United States and Canada, open range is rangeland where cattle roam freely regardless of land ownership. Where there are \"open range\" laws, those wanting to keep animals off their property must erect a fence to keep animals out; this applies to public roads as well. Land in open range that is designated as part of a \"herd district\" reverses liabilities, requiring an animal's owner to fence it in or otherwise keep it on the person's own property. Most eastern states and jurisdictions in Canada require owners to fence in or herd their livestock."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Muddy_Water_Red_desert.jpg/330px-Muddy_Water_Red_desert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Open_range","wikidata":"Q7096405"},{"title":"Open Range (2003 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Open Range is a 2003 American revisionist Western film directed and co-produced by Kevin Costner, written by Craig Storper and based on the novel The Open Range Men by Lauran Paine. It stars Robert Duvall and Costner, with Annette Bening, Michael Gambon, and Michael Jeter appearing in supporting roles. It presents a range war that happens when free-grazing herder \"Boss\" Spearman (Duvall) and his cowboys enter the Montana territory of cattle baron Denton Baxter (Gambon)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/02/Open_range_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Open_Range_(2003_film)","wikidata":"Q1546370"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/2014-08-09_12_07_15_Open_Range_sign_along_southbound_U.S._Route_93_in_far_northern_Lincoln_County%2C_Nevada.JPG/500px-2014-08-09_12_07_15_Open_Range_sign_along_southbound_U.S._Route_93_in_far_northern_Lincoln_County%2C_Nevada.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/2014-08-09_12_07_15_Open_Range_sign_along_southbound_U.S._Route_93_in_far_northern_Lincoln_County%2C_Nevada.JPG/1280px-2014-08-09_12_07_15_Open_Range_sign_along_southbound_U.S._Route_93_in_far_northern_Lincoln_County%2C_Nevada.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/2014-08-09_12_07_15_Open_Range_sign_along_southbound_U.S._Route_93_in_far_northern_Lincoln_County%2C_Nevada.JPG/500px-2014-08-09_12_07_15_Open_Range_sign_along_southbound_U.S._Route_93_in_far_northern_Lincoln_County%2C_Nevada.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2014-08-09_12_07_15_Open_Range_sign_along_southbound_U.S._Route_93_in_far_northern_Lincoln_County%2C_Nevada.JPG"},{